<title>USA: International Business Machines Q3 oper net.</title>
<headline>International Business Machines Q3 oper net.</headline>
<dateline>ARMONK, N.Y. 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Oper shr		   $2.45		    $2.30</p>
<p> Oper net	     1,285,000		1,302,000</p>
<p> Revs		  18,062,000	     16,754,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 521,800		  564,600</p>
<p>	 (All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1995 Q3 and nine months exclude charge of $1.84 billion, or $3.26 per share, to write off costs related to the acquisition of Lotus Development Corp in July 1995.</p>
<p>1996 Q3 First Call consensus estimate was $2.43/shr.  </p>
<p>	   9  MONTHS</p>
<p> Oper shr		   $7.16		    $7.39</p>
<p> Oper net	     3,841,000		4,307,000</p>
<p> Revs		  52,804,000	     50,020,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 533,300		  575,100</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 nine months excludes charge of $435 million, or $0.80 per share, to write off acquisition-related costs of Tivoli Systems Inc and Object Technology International Inc.</p>
<p>Full company name is International Business Machines Corp.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1736</p>
